# L §5.16 A random number of items (PL-22): "a bounded index of slots, read by a range that ends at the draw ... A draw
# past the last slot ... is refused on that path (RUN-KEY, §4.2), and at load where load sees the draw's support
# exceed the index (LOAD-RANDOM)"; L §8.3 `the draw <x> can exceed the last slot of <index>`. n is a poisson draw,
# whose support has no last value, over three slots: refused at load. (The range is written `1 .. n step 1`, as L
# §5.16's example is since round 17: a draw of a dist with no unit is a num, and L §5.11 refuses a range of quantities
# without a step.)
=== m.tally
model t
  tally 2
  on 2026-12-31
  start 2026-01-01
  end 2026-12-31

source src "s"
index slots = int 1..3
input lam: num
input cost[k in slots]: num
input n: dist
def total: num = sum(cost[k] for k in 1 .. n step 1)

ask q: mean(total) paths 20 seed 1

version v
  cite src
  governs always
  known 2026-01-01
  lam = 1
  cost[*] = 2
  n = poisson(lam)
=== expect
refused: LOAD-RANDOM the draw n can exceed the last slot of slots ...
